      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Patellofemoral joint forces and pressures were measured in a cadaver model during intramedullary nailing of the tibia. A significant increase in contact pressures was found at the lateral facet of the patellofemoral articulation using the medial paratendinous approach (P = 0.01) and at the medial facet when using the trans-patellar tendon approach (P = 0.001) to the proximal tibia. Increased contact pressures at the patello-femoral joint may result in chondral injury, which in turn may cause anterior knee pain, a common complication of tibial nailing."},
